      "writtenOn": "2025-08-04T20:37:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Added a GM that draws a gradient image with height \u003e 32768 and scales it down.From compilers I\u0027ve seen, behavior for casting floats greater than INT_MAX to ints can result in INT_MAX or INT_MIN. I don\u0027t think this would have a noticeable difference in results because after the cast, we subtract 32768. For INT_MIN results, this underflows back to only be off by 1 of the INT_MAX case. But again, this behavior is undefined so this would catch other behaviors of the cast.",
